<h1>Mike Quigley</h1>
<p>Candidate for Mayor, Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027</p>
<p><a href="https://www.quigleyforchicago.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.quigleyforchicago.com/priorities" rel="nofollow noopener">Mike Quigley&#39;s campaign has published plans for housing, public safety, and the city budget. Tap here to read them on his site, then come back to comment.</a></p>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Housing: Build or preserve 50,000 homes in four years. Allow four-flats, courtyard buildings, and backyard units across the city, and send TIF money to affordable housing. Quigley rejects new rent restrictions.</p>
<p>Police: Move 600 officers from desk jobs back to patrol instead of hiring 1,000 more, cap overtime, and replace eight oversight bodies with one elected board.</p>
<p>Prevention: Mental health teams on crisis calls, reopened neighborhood mental health clinics, and more funding for violence intervention groups.</p>
<p>Budget: Start with $530 million to $1.3 billion in yearly savings that a city-paid report already identified.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>Only Quigley: A housing target, 50,000 homes. Cardenas would legalize the same building types without a number.</p>
<p>Renters: Quigley rejects new rent restrictions. Brewer and Cardenas stress protecting renters from displacement.</p>
<p>Mental health: Holberg, Quigley, and Carlisle would send mental health teams to crisis calls. Quigley and Carlisle would also reopen neighborhood mental health clinics.</p>
<p>Not covered so far: Schools and transit. Holberg, Kelly, Wilson, Carlisle, and Su address both.</p>
